  "sourceScopeNotes": [
    "379: actions and background conditions both matter; education differs from equipment improvement; no injury does not establish quality; classifications do not exhaust causes or justify deleting information.",
    "380: expected sequence differs from actual instruction; full IDs rather than matching suffix; attention narrowing is not simply poor effort; clear front view does not verify footing/behind.",
    "381: repeated similar boxes may change model midstream; unfamiliar work does not imply universal incompetence; past hazard experience must match current conditions; silence/nodding/no questions do not prove understanding.",
    "382: familiarity/prior no-failure does not replace today checks; delays do not justify skipped inspection; group approval does not establish safe conditions; workload/order/overlap require management review rather than reliance on endurance.",
    "383: hearing differs from understanding; repeat-back is not merely repeating sounds; affirmative replies do not prove target agreement; leader message does not establish all workers/new shift informed; undated changes remain uncertain.",
    "384: reflex/unplanned movement must be considered; dropping objects example is not a recommendation; emergency roles/contacts shared in advance rather than assuming spontaneous correct decisions; changed paths require emergency-information updates.",
    "385: age alone does not determine capability; eyesight/function difficulties also involve environment/display/lighting; fatigue involves both sleep and workload/rest; health changes go through appropriate contacts without relying on endurance or bystander speculation."
